# Force LF line endings everywhere, regardless of what a given machine's
# Git core.autocrlf setting does. This matters most for run.sh - it's a
# bash script with a #!/usr/bin/with-contenv bashio shebang, and if that
# line ever gets checked out with CRLF endings (e.g. on Windows with
# autocrlf=true), the container fails to start entirely, since the shell
# looks for a program literally named "bashio\r".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files - never touch these regardless of the above.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
